For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

INSTRUMENT: a device that requires skill for proper use.
INTERN: an advanced student or graduate in medicine gaining supervised practical experience (`houseman' is a British term).
IONIC: the dialect of Ancient Greek spoken and written in Attica and Athens and Ionia.
ISOTOPE: one of two or more atoms with the same atomic number but with different numbers of neutrons.
ITEM: a distinct part that can be specified separately in a group of things that could be enumerated on a list.
ITSELF: The neuter reflexive pronoun of It.
